Aurora-A interacts with and phosphorylates ERalpha
To determine the mechanism by which Aurora-A induces ERalpha transactivation activity, we initially performed co-immunoprecipitation in MDA-MB-231 cells following transfection of GFP-ERalpha and HA-Aurora-A. Figure 4c shows that HA-Aurora-A interacted with GFP-ERalpha. We next examined if endogenous ERalpha and Aurora-A forms a complex. Co-immunoprecipitation was carried out in MCF7-TamR cells, which express elevated Aurora-A and ERalpha (Figure 1a). As shown in Figure 4d, ERalpha was readily detected in Aurora-A immunoprecipitates and vice versa. Furthermore, GST-pull down assay revealed that GST-Aurora-A but not GST could pull-down the recombinant ERalpha (Figure 4e). These data indicate that Aurora-A directly binds to ERalpha. To determine if Aurora-A co

